<pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.18" change_id="I8a7e1afc25da0aabf77d6acff48830409c427c0e" commit="9f6ed159c56db5970fce3a47afecba096d92939e" commit_message="FROMLIST: ASoC: nau8825: extend FLL functions  Extend FLL clock source from MCLK/BCLK/FS. Modify FLL calculation and parameter setting.  Signed-off-by: John Hsu &lt;KCHSU0@nuvoton.com&gt; (am from http://www.spinics.net/lists/alsa-devel/msg44796.html)  BUG=chrome-os-partner:49515 TEST=with the whole series applied, audio works on SKL.  Change-Id: I8a7e1afc25da0aabf77d6acff48830409c427c0e Signed-off-by: Yong Zhi &lt;yong.zhi@intel.com&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/322466 Commit-Ready: Ben Zhang &lt;benzh@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Ben Zhang &lt;benzh@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Ben Zhang &lt;benzh@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="322466" owner_email="yong.zhi@intel.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="4" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/66/322466/4" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.18" change_id="Ibe3a55cb0954a8772da6d1467de2349dba42fbcf" commit="2ac0298a8d9d3aa344fadcf18809fd61cf4e6a58" commit_message="FROMLIST: ASoC: nau8825: add power management S3 solution  This patch is to fix interrupt fails when resume back. In solution, we add IRQ re-initiation, and reconstruct suspend and resume with set_bias_level function.  Signed-off-by: John Hsu &lt;KCHSU0@nuvoton.com&gt; (am from http://www.spinics.net/lists/alsa-devel/msg44993.html)  BUG=chrome-os-partner:49523 TEST=with the whole series applied, audio works on SKL.  Change-Id: Ibe3a55cb0954a8772da6d1467de2349dba42fbcf Signed-off-by: Yong Zhi &lt;yong.zhi@intel.com&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/322623 Commit-Ready: Ben Zhang &lt;benzh@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Ben Zhang &lt;benzh@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Ben Zhang &lt;benzh@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="322623" owner_email="yong.zhi@intel.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="3" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/23/322623/3" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.18" change_id="I540fbe6ecb7f56e8fe2ae851c5a83707019b393c" commit="354adfd3384938f33afa3250d4a5e53e9a32d59d" commit_message="FROMLIST: ASoC: nau8825: reduce standby power consumption  Fix unnecessary widget power up when standby; And decrease internal clock frequency to save power.  Signed-off-by: John Hsu &lt;KCHSU0@nuvoton.com&gt; (am from http://www.spinics.net/lists/alsa-devel/msg45214.html)  BUG=chrome-os-partner:49554 TEST=with the whole series applied, audio works on SKL.  Change-Id: I540fbe6ecb7f56e8fe2ae851c5a83707019b393c Signed-off-by: Yong Zhi &lt;yong.zhi@intel.com&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/322634 Commit-Ready: Ben Zhang &lt;benzh@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Ben Zhang &lt;benzh@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Ben Zhang &lt;benzh@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="322634" owner_email="yong.zhi@intel.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="3" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/34/322634/3" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.14" change_id="I597cc7060acd069c1fce6bc5d9a137b584a3d24d" commit="8a1a40cfc64813dae6390f38f766fdecb43f6968" commit_message="CHROMIUM: mali: drm_reservation_cb_done after reservation_object_add_shared_fence  In general it looks like it's wise to call reservation_object_add_shared_fence() _before_ calling drm_reservation_cb_done().  The difference should really only matter on PREEMPT kernels since drm_reservation_cb_done() can only ever do schedule_work() which should do nothing until we give up the current CPU (unless PREEMPT).  Said another way: before PREEMPT the two orderings were equivalent.  Now they're not.  Now that we've got PREEMPT let's do it right.  In this particular case presumably the callback could somehow end up NULLing out &quot;katom-&gt;rendered_fence&quot; and we'd end up with the same type of problem that we fixed in (&quot;drm: rockchip: Add the shared fence before calling the callback&quot;).  In testing we haven't seen the katom-&gt;rendered_fence actually become NULL, but it seems better not to tempt fate.  BUG=chromium:586711 TEST=See steps in bug  Change-Id: I597cc7060acd069c1fce6bc5d9a137b584a3d24d Signed-off-by: Douglas Anderson &lt;dianders@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/329391 Reviewed-by: Stéphane Marchesin &lt;marcheu@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="329391" owner_email="dianders@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/91/329391/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.14" change_id="I7af88cfd0e98e87cfcd0c20c263cccf3e04d7d45" commit="f681fa097d0cf5f9dc7efe9f4c9e67da07c05811" commit_message="CHROMIUM: reservation: WARN_ON for NULL fence when adding shared fence  We just got done debugging a problem where &quot;fence&quot; was being passed as NULL to reservation_object_add_shared_fence().  It was hard to debug because the problem showed up much later.  We ended up with a trace that looked like this (note that this is in a kernel with non-upstreamed kbase):  (__dabt_svc) from (reservation_object_get_fences_rcu+0x144/0x260) (reservation_object_get_fences_rcu) from (drm_reservation_cb_add+0x4c/0x17c) (drm_reservation_cb_add) from (jd_submit_atom+0xa74/0xfb0) (jd_submit_atom) from (kbase_jd_submit+0x2a0/0x330) (kbase_jd_submit) from (kbase_ioctl+0x638/0xaa0) (kbase_ioctl) from  (do_vfs_ioctl+0x494/0x5a8) (do_vfs_ioctl) from  (SyS_ioctl+0x5c/0x84) (SyS_ioctl) from  (__sys_trace_return+0x0/0x28)  Specifically note that fence_get_rcu(), unlike fence_get() and fence_put(), doesn't check for a NULL fence.  Presumably that's because a NULL fence isn't valid in this case.  As further evidence that shared fences shouldn't be NULL you can see the following in reservation_object_get_fences_rcu() for an exclusive fence:    if (!fence_excl || fence_get_rcu(fence_excl))  ...but this for a shared fence (no NULL check):    if (fence_get_rcu(shared[i]))  Let's add a WARN_ON for a NULL shared fence for now.  Technically it might be better to add a BUG_ON and crash sooner, but just in case I'm mistaken and it's valid to have a NULL shared fence in some strange case we'll use WARN_ON.  ...and people hate BUG_ON anyway.  Even better would be to do something sane when we see a NULL shared fence, though I'm not sure what that is.  BUG=chromium:586711 TEST=Don't see the WARN_ON.  Change-Id: I7af88cfd0e98e87cfcd0c20c263cccf3e04d7d45 Signed-off-by: Douglas Anderson &lt;dianders@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/329400 Reviewed-by: Stéphane Marchesin &lt;marcheu@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="329400" owner_email="dianders@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/00/329400/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.18" change_id="I3860e24b0344def6452669a6f6f709f8f125e0bd" commit="e96c4b1d05bf3062b08003a4d3671b0c35c7643a" commit_message="UPSTREAM: ASoC: mediatek: remove soft reset and add second I2S clock  To improve I2S flow, this patch removes soft reset and adds second I2S clock to use.  Signed-off-by: PC Liao &lt;pc.liao@mediatek.com&gt; Signed-off-by: Mark Brown &lt;broonie@kernel.org&gt; (cherry picked from commit 4d7cb66c8f9db37ffa2a72cc9b9233ae82e94d7e)  BUG=chrome-os-partner:49521 TEST=oak-rev4, run audio_AudioBasicExternalMicrophone --iteration=100  Change-Id: I3860e24b0344def6452669a6f6f709f8f125e0bd Signed-off-by: PC Liao &lt;pc.liao@mediatek.com&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/327512 Reviewed-by: Daniel Kurtz &lt;djkurtz@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Nicolas Boichat &lt;drinkcat@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="327512" owner_email="pc.liao@mediatek.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/12/327512/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.18" change_id="Ib6804bbbde388830d8359245fe13bbb0f2bb36ba" commit="c0d3991dc345b848ded724d094ba92b759761124" commit_message="UPSTREAM: ASoC: mediatek: Add I03/I04 widgets and corresponding routes  Add these widgets to allow another path from I2S input.  Signed-off-by: Koro Chen &lt;koro.chen@mediatek.com&gt; Signed-off-by: PC Liao &lt;pc.liao@mediatek.com&gt; Signed-off-by: Mark Brown &lt;broonie@kernel.org&gt; (cherry picked from commit 84f3a52421a41d0b129b519da9f39fcfb336a840)  BUG=chrome-os-partner:50078 TEST=oak-rev6, check register setting by amixer &quot;O09 I03 Switch&quot; and &quot;O10 I04 Switch&quot;  Change-Id: Ib6804bbbde388830d8359245fe13bbb0f2bb36ba Signed-off-by: Koro Chen &lt;koro.chen@mediatek.com&gt; Signed-off-by: PC Liao &lt;pc.liao@mediatek.com&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/319979 Reviewed-by: Daniel Kurtz &lt;djkurtz@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Nicolas Boichat &lt;drinkcat@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="319979" owner_email="koro.chen@mediatek.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="4" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/79/319979/4" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I6689cdbb6d213c6dc179f21bd7250c8db028e986" commit="2122ca959b21382c1e113a91acd38e18bc468ca9" commit_message="[backlight] Extract backlight syspath for overwritting  We may usually have the same logic of SetBacklightBrightness function. So just extract the syspath for overwritting. It will be easy to implement this function for different board.  BUG=None TEST=Test it on android device  Change-Id: I6689cdbb6d213c6dc179f21bd7250c8db028e986 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/328918 Commit-Ready: Hsu Wei-Cheng &lt;mojahsu@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Hsu Wei-Cheng &lt;mojahsu@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Hung-Te Lin &lt;hungte@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="328918" owner_email="mojahsu@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/platform/factory" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/factory" ref="refs/changes/18/328918/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-2015.07" change_id="I328b074b4f56ebe3caa8952ce3df7f834c1cf40f" commit="4f657d81e36805eb7bca372647b02b75e7373fbd" commit_message="Skylake boards: Enabling HWP  This patch provides config options to enable/disable Intel SST.  BUG=chrome-os-partner:47517 BRANCH=None TEST=Booted kunimitsu/lars, verified HWP driver load successfully.  CQ-DEPEND=CL:313107  Change-Id: I328b074b4f56ebe3caa8952ce3df7f834c1cf40f Signed-off-by: Robbie Zhang &lt;robbie.zhang@intel.com&gt; Signed-off-by: Subrata Banik &lt;subrata.banik@intel.com&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/326650 Tested-by: Wenkai Du &lt;wenkai.du@intel.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Benson Leung &lt;bleung@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="326650" owner_email="subrata.banik@intel.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="7" project="chromiumos/third_party/coreboot" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/coreboot" ref="refs/changes/50/326650/7" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Iab021efcbfd1b7077fda813752a16499c5f01fc0" commit="f5cae466d967380565bea73a648bbe877f9fb4be" commit_message="dut: Implement sysfs thermal component  1. Add SysFSThermal class. 2. Rename old Thermal class to ECToolThermal.  BUG=none TEST=Run thermal_load test.  Change-Id: Iab021efcbfd1b7077fda813752a16499c5f01fc0 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/324731 Commit-Ready: Ting Shen &lt;phoenixshen@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Ting Shen &lt;phoenixshen@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Hung-Te Lin &lt;hungte@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="1" gerrit_number="324731" owner_email="phoenixshen@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="5" project="chromiumos/platform/factory" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/factory" ref="refs/changes/31/324731/5" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I0ef9b04ead212d8dedb90b616a11a0d1f91f6905" commit="f952755a7155c092f835bc45fd93353c09bb6a97" commit_message="Preserve RW_NVRAM section when doing a full image update  With our classical NVRAM solutions (CMOS and EC), NVRAM contents are automatically preserved across firmware updates. Some FAFT tests and possibly other processes rely on this. With the newly-introduced flash-backed NVRAM (only on boards using updater5.sh, as far as I know), recovery firmware updates that write the whole image will also overwrite the NVRAM section (causing previous state to be lost and crossystem to fail until after the next reboot since the section can only be properly reinitialized from firmware).  Therefore, this patch introduces code to preserve the contents of the RW_NVRAM section (if it exists), similar to what was already done with the VPD and the GBB flags.  BUG=chrome-os-partner:47461 TEST=Run 'chromeos-firmwareupdate --mode=recovery' on Oak, confirm that crossystem doesn't throw errors and still shows the same (non-default) NVRAM contents as before the update. Run 'chromeos-firmwareupdate --mode=recovery --debug' on Jerry, confirm that it still works and I see &quot;System doesn't have flash NVRAM. Skip.&quot; message.  Change-Id: I0ef9b04ead212d8dedb90b616a11a0d1f91f6905 Signed-off-by: Julius Werner &lt;jwerner@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/319600 Reviewed-by: Hung-Te Lin &lt;hungte@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Randall Spangler &lt;rspangler@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="319600" owner_email="jwerner@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="3" project="chromiumos/platform/firmware" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/firmware" ref="refs/changes/00/319600/3" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.18" change_id="Ia49574bc87745e9ce48781cb8b67e518240ae25d" commit="330cad7b34de38ba2e41bcbd7591eab290aedcb5" commit_message="CHROMIUM: drm/img-rogue: Add missing PDUMP files  The build was failing when both DRM_POWERVR_ROGUE_PDUMP and DRM_POWERVR_ROGUE_KERNEL_SRVINIT were enabled.  This change adds the files that implement the missing features.  BUG=chromium:583462 TEST=Build with the above build options enabled and disabled.      Build normally and run webgl aquarium.  Change-Id: Ia49574bc87745e9ce48781cb8b67e518240ae25d Signed-off-by: Rufus Hamade &lt;rufus.hamade@imgtec.com&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/328992 Commit-Ready: Daniel Kurtz &lt;djkurtz@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Daniel Kurtz &lt;djkurtz@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Guenter Roeck &lt;groeck@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Daniel Kurtz &lt;djkurtz@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="328992" owner_email="rufus.hamade@imgtec.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/92/328992/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><lkgm version="7967.0.0-rc1"/></manifest>